#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:92
msgid "Cascading Inputs"
msgstr "Entradas en cascada"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:94
msgid ""
"One powerful facet of |morpheus| Inputs is the ability to present users "
"with different lists of input options based on their selections in other "
"Inputs within the same wizard or modal. One common example, which is "
"fully illustrated in this section, is to have a user select:"
msgstr "One powerful facet de |morpheus| Inputs es el/la ability a present users con diferente lists de input options based en their selections en otro/otra Inputs dentro de el/la mismo/misma wizard o modal. One common example, el/la cual es fully illustrated en este/esta section, es a tienen un/una user select:"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:96
msgid "The Group they wish to provision into..."
msgstr "The Group they wish to provision into..."

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:97
msgid ""
"Then select the target Cloud from a list limited to Clouds which are in "
"the selected Group..."
msgstr "Then select el/la target Nube desde un/una list limited a Nubes el/la cual son en el/la seleccionado/seleccionada Grupo..."

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:98
msgid ""
"Then select the target network from a list limited to networks which are "
"available to the selected Cloud *and* Group"
msgstr "Then select el/la target network desde un/una list limited a networks el/la cual son disponible a el/la seleccionado/seleccionada Nube *and* Grupo"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:100
msgid ""
"To set this up, we will first configure our Inputs (custom option fields "
"that can be applied to Instance Types and other |morpheus| constructs) "
"and Option Lists (dynamic lists of possible choices which can be "
"associated with Inputs and presented in a dropdown or typeahead format). "
"Once the custom options are configured, we will associate them with a new"
" service catalog item and take a look at how the user would interact with"
" them."
msgstr "To set this up, we will first configure our Inputs (custom option fields that can be applied to Tipos de instancia and other |morpheus| constructs) and Listas de opciones (dynamic lists of possible choices which puede ser associated with Inputs and presented in a dropdown or typeahead format). Once the custom options are configured, we will associate them with a new service catalog item and take a look at how the user would interact with them."

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:103
msgid "Group Custom Options"
msgstr "Opciones personalizadas de grupo"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:105
msgid ""
"To begin, we will create a new `Option List "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/provisioning/library/library.html"
"#option-lists>`_ In this case, we will select type of \"Morpheus Api\" "
"which will populate the list based on a call to the internal |morpheus| "
"API. Option Lists can also be populated by calls to external REST APIs or"
" even from static lists that you enter manually. When dynamically "
"populating Option Lists, whether via |morpheus| API or an external API, "
"translation and/or request scripts may be needed to prepare the request "
"or translate the results. More on that as we build out the example."
msgstr "To begin, we será/n create un/una nuevo/nueva `Lista de opciones <https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/provisioning/library/library.html#option-lists>`_ In este/esta case, we será/n select type de \"Morpheus Api\" el/la cual será/n populate el/la list based en un/una call a el/la internal |morpheus| API. Listas de opciones puede/n también be populated por calls a external REST APIs o even desde static lists ese/esa you enter manually. Cuando dynamically populating Listas de opciones, whether via |morpheus| API o un/una external API, translation and/or request scripts puede/n be needed a prepare el/la request o translate el/la results. More en ese/esa como we build fuera el/la example."

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:107
msgid ""
"I have called my Option List \"Groups\" and selected \"Groups\" from the "
"OPTION LIST menu. This simply indicates that Groups are the construct we "
"want to call into our list from |morpheus| API. In this case, we want to "
"present a list of all Groups to the user by their name and pass the Group"
" database ID in the background. Since it is common to create Option Lists"
" from |morpheus| API where the construct name is displayed to the user "
"and the ID is passed, we actually do not need to input any translation "
"scripts in this case. However, I will include a translation script here "
"which does the same thing simply to provide more clarity to the example. "
"|morpheus| `Option List documentation "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/library/options/option_lists.html>`_"
" includes additional details on available translation script inputs and "
"which are available without translation as a convenience feature."
msgstr "I tienen called my Lista de opciones \"Grupos\" y seleccionado/seleccionada \"Grupos\" desde el/la OPTION LIST menu. Este/Esta simply indicates ese/esa Grupos son el/la construct we want a call en our list desde |morpheus| API. In este/esta case, we want a present un/una list de todos/todas Grupos a el/la user por their name y pass el/la Grupo database ID en el/la background. Since it es common a create Listas de opciones desde |morpheus| API donde el/la construct name es displayed a el/la user y el/la ID es passed, we actually do ningún need a input cualquier translation scripts en este/esta case. However, I será/n include un/una translation script here el/la cual does el/la mismo/misma thing simply a provide más clarity a el/la example. |morpheus| `Lista de opciones documentation <https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/library/options/option_lists.html>`_ includes additional details en disponible translation script inputs y el/la cual son disponible sin translation como un/una convenience feature."

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:109
msgid ""
"for (var x = 0; x < data.length; x++) {\n"
"  results.push({name: data[x].name, value:data[x].id});\n"
"}"
msgstr "for (var x = 0; x < data.length; x++) {\\n  results.push({name: data[x].name, value:data[x].id});\\n}"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:115
msgid ""
"After saving the Option List, create the Input that presents the list we "
"just created. I gave my Input the name of \"Selected Group\", field name "
"of \"selectedGroup\", and label of \"Group\". For type, choose \"Select "
"List\" and a new field will appear at the bottom of the modal where we "
"can select the Option List we just created. With this configuration, the "
"Input will present as a dropdown list containing the options called from "
"our Option List."
msgstr "Después de saving el/la Lista de opciones, create el/la Input ese/esa presents el/la list we just created. I gave my Input el/la name de \"Selected Grupo\", field name de \"selectedGrupo\", y label de \"Grupo\". For type, choose \"Select List\" y un/una nuevo/nueva field será/n appear en el/la bottom de el/la modal donde we puede/n select el/la Lista de opciones we just created. With este/esta configuration, el/la Input será/n present como un/una dropdown list containing el/la options called desde our Lista de opciones."

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:118
msgid "Cloud Custom Options"
msgstr "Opciones personalizadas de nube"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:120
msgid ""
"Adding the Option List and Input for Clouds will be similar to the prior "
"step with the exception that we will be including a request script which "
"effectively filters the list of available Clouds to only those associated"
" with the selected group. Follow the same process to start a new Option "
"List, I have configured mine as follows:"
msgstr "Adding el/la Lista de opciones y Input para Nubes será/n be similar a el/la prior step con el/la exception ese/esa we será/n be including un/una request script el/la cual effectively filters el/la list de disponible Nubes a solo esos/esas asociado/asociada con el/la seleccionado/seleccionada group. Follow el/la mismo/misma process a start un/una nuevo/nueva Lista de opciones, I tienen configurado/configurada mine como follows:"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:122
msgid "**NAME:** Parsed Clouds"
msgstr "**NAME:** Parsed Nubes"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:123
#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:161
msgid "**TYPE:** Morpheus Api"
msgstr "**TYPE:** Morpheus Api"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:124
msgid "**OPTION LIST:** Clouds"
msgstr "**OPTION LIST:** Nubes"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:126
msgid ""
"We also need a request script that loads the ``siteId`` attribute of the "
"``results`` variable with the Group ID if the user has made a group "
"selection. Essentially it appends this input as a query parameter to the "
"API call, calling (for example) ``./api/clouds?siteId=1`` rather than "
"``.../api/clouds``. It should be similar to the script below. Note that "
"we are referencing the ``selectedGroup`` field name we created previously"
" and that a \"site\" is the term for Groups in the |morpheus| database."
msgstr "We también need un/una request script ese/esa loads el/la ``siteId`` attribute de el/la ``results`` variable con el/la Grupo ID si el/la user tiene made un/una group selection. Essentially it appends este/esta input como un/una query parameter a el/la API call, calling (for example) ``./api/clouds?siteId=1`` rather than ``.../api/clouds``. It debería/n be similar a el/la script below. Note ese/esa we son referencing el/la ``selectedGrupo`` field name we creado/creada previously y ese/esa un/una \"site\" es el/la term para Grupos en el/la |morpheus| database."

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:128
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"if (input.selectedGroup) {\n"
"  results.siteId = input.selectedGroup\n"
"}"
msgstr "if (input.selectedGroup) {\\n  results.siteId = input.selectedGroup\\n}"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:134
msgid ""
"We also need a translation script which will be identical to the one used"
" previously with the exception that if there is no input on the "
"``selectedGroups`` field, nothing will be displayed for the Clouds "
"option."
msgstr "We también need un/una translation script el/la cual será/n be identical a el/la one utilizado/utilizada previously con el/la exception ese/esa si there es ningún input en el/la ``selectedGrupos`` field, nothing será/n be displayed para el/la Nubes option."

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:136
msgid ""
"if (input.selectedGroup) {\n"
"for (var x = 0; x < data.length; x++) {\n"
"    results.push({name:data[x].name, value:data[x].id});\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr "if (input.selectedGroup) {\\nfor (var x = 0; x < data.length; x++) {\\n    results.push({name:data[x].name, value:data[x].id});\\n  }\\n}"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:144
msgid ""
"We also need to create an Input to house this Option List. This process "
"will be very similar to creating the previous Input except that we need "
"to set selectedGroup as the Dependent Field. Setting a dependent field on"
" an Input will trigger it to reload each time a selection is made in the "
"indicated option. My configuration is as follows:"
msgstr "We también need a create un/una Input a house este/esta Lista de opciones. Este/Esta process será/n be very similar a creating el/la anterior Input except ese/esa we need a establecido/establecida selectedGrupo como el/la Dependent Field. Setting un/una dependent field en un/una Input será/n trigger it a reload cada time un/una selection es made en el/la indicated option. My configuration es como follows:"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:146
msgid "**NAME:** Parsed Cloud"
msgstr "**NAME:** Parsed Nube"

#: ../../library/options/option_types.rst:147
msgid "**FIELD NAME:** parsedCloud"
